{"h":3395,"w":2400,"lines":[{"h":0.008720930389296444,"t":"1718867188","c":0.30000001192092896,"x":0.7716049391467531,"y":0.046511627815394085,"w":0.069958845774332645},{"c":1,"t":"READING PASSAGE 2","x":0.1008230390430009,"y":0.097383720794351092,"w":0.29012346903483077,"h":0.01453488398216074},{"y":0.13221436957039645,"c":1,"h":0.016041444524578563,"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading","x":0.10288066774952029,"w":0.77160491943359377},{"y":0.14811542989978521,"w":0.15843621571858724,"t":"Passage 2 below.","h":0.016195524146054185,"c":1,"x":0.10288065740133741},{"t":"A second attempt at domesticating the tomato","x":0.17283949346801725,"y":0.1904069771048148,"c":1,"w":0.63786010742187504,"h":0.021901621554568984},{"w":0.72427983601888024,"x":0.14197530822393142,"y":0.22819767428587678,"t":"It took at least 3,000 years for humans to learn how to domesticate the wild tomato","c":1,"h":0.01453488398216074},{"x":0.14403291951333122,"t":"and cultivate it for food. Now two separate teams in Brazil and China have done it all","c":1,"w":0.7366255187988282,"h":0.014723203769140158,"y":0.24411071846411436},{"t":"over again in less than three years. And they have done it better in some ways, as","w":0.71202850341796875,"x":0.14810123873002945,"y":0.25998738388654963,"h":0.016252110507097961,"c":1},{"h":0.013081395583944722,"w":0.71810699462890615,"x":0.14609053550417958,"y":0.27906976732241628,"t":"the re-domesticated tomatoes are more nutritious than the ones we eat at present.","c":1},{"w":0.70164606730143231,"h":0.016027748233718886,"c":1,"x":0.14609054649208833,"t":"This approach relies on the revolutionary CRISPR genome editing technique, in","y":0.30523255799347171},{"c":1,"t":"which changes are deliberately made to the DNA of a living cell, allowing genetic","x":0.1440329251912334,"w":0.71193415323893228,"y":0.32122093049064326,"h":0.015988371257085521},{"t":"material to be added, removed or altered. The technique could not only improve","h":0.016017476296396715,"c":1,"x":0.14403291608008714,"y":0.33863368663444038,"w":0.70370371500651041},{"y":0.35453474678308639,"h":0.016195524146054296,"t":"existing crops, but could also be used to turn thousands of wild plants into useful","x":0.14403291962538997,"w":0.71193415323893228,"c":1},{"w":0.70781890869140629,"t":"and appealing foods. In fact, a third team in the US has already begun to do this","y":0.37209302310969239,"x":0.14403293238489426,"h":0.016010628150966877,"c":1},{"y":0.38571826255225206,"h":0.0179308598117357,"c":1,"t":"with a relative of the tomato called the groundcherry.","w":0.46328308105468752,"x":0.14596661741444852},{"w":0.016460905075073237,"h":0.013081395583944722,"x":0.10082304530196955,"y":0.58139534861064401,"c":1,"t":"B"},{"y":0.41715116265804109,"t":"This tast-track domestication could help make the world's tood supply healthier and","x":0.14403291134720178,"w":0.73456792195638021,"h":0.01453488398216074,"c":1},{"t":"far more resistant to diseases, such as the rust fungus devastating wheat crops.","y":0.43313953473712652,"x":0.14197530191988278,"w":0.70987655639648439,"h":0.01598837238037687,"c":1},{"w":0.72222223917643225,"x":0.14609052644663109,"y":0.45930232543038441,"h":0.01598837238037687,"t":"'This could transform what we eat,' says Jorg Kudla at the University of Munster in","c":1},{"c":1,"t":"Germany, a member of the Brazilian team. 'There are 50,000 edible plants in the","x":0.1440329151084444,"y":0.47673733831656784,"w":0.70987655639648439,"h":0.015995219964161089},{"x":0.14390256660006609,"y":0.49122069973300064,"w":0.55176742553710945,"c":1,"t":"world, but 90 percent of our energy comes from just 15 crops.'","h":0.020488550300732933},{"w":0.73273996988932288,"y":0.51750628133000598,"t":"'We can now mimic the known domestication course of major crops like rice, maize,","c":1,"h":0.019170215188825113,"x":0.14394226712949301},{"x":0.14398419768013487,"c":1,"t":"sorghum or others,' says Caixia Gao of the Chinese Academy of Sciences in Beijing.","y":0.53597387941041563,"h":0.017844110270973101,"w":0.73879419962565107},{"c":1,"y":0.55228475294947177,"h":0.018731721579256178,"t":"\"Then we might try to domesticate plants that have never been domesticated.'","w":0.68741770426432292,"x":0.14398496259698704},{"y":0.5797465148806884,"t":"Wild tomatoes, which are native to the Andes region in South America, produce","w":0.7017882283528647,"x":0.1419084063444554,"h":0.017893648540734941,"c":1},{"x":0.14403292515210164,"y":0.59883720915534544,"h":0.016003780005537038,"w":0.69958847045898431,"c":1,"t":"pea-sized fruits. Over many generations, peoples such as the Aztecs and Incas"},{"y":0.61317205362810956,"w":0.69147343953450524,"x":0.14397388432721717,"h":0.018763543298584207,"t":"transformed the plant by selecting and breeding plants with mutations* in their","c":1},{"w":0.62153925577799485,"c":1,"t":"genetic structure, which resulted in desirable traits such as larger fruit.","y":0.62984512508350221,"x":0.14394766774144899,"h":0.018901577827085125},{"h":0.017367343880122066,"c":1,"t":"But every time a single plant with a mutation is taken from a larger population for","y":0.65837334570556172,"x":0.14399577285372089,"w":0.71202626546223968},{"x":0.1460905464946749,"y":0.67579505307950427,"h":0.014723203769140158,"w":0.70164606730143231,"c":1,"t":"breeding, much genetic diversity is lost. And sometimes the desirable mutations"},{"x":0.14392777774108709,"w":0.64836085001627597,"h":0.020147530293998184,"c":1,"y":0.69037854228428697,"t":"come with less desirable traits. For instance, the tomato strains grown for"},{"w":0.40123456319173179,"t":"supermarkets have lost much of their flavour.","x":0.14403292407692581,"c":1,"y":0.70930232544514638,"h":0.01453488398216074},{"h":0.015960482180609969,"x":0.14808906926161361,"y":0.73551156634082815,"c":1,"t":"By comparing the genomes of modern plants to those of their wild relatives,","w":0.66472686767578126},{"w":0.70586558024088542,"y":0.75286427378078657,"x":0.14398177608327833,"t":"biologists have been working out what genetic changes occurred as plants were","h":0.017090272847277821,"c":1},{"t":"domesticated. The teams in Brazil and China have now used this knowledge to","w":0.69547322591145833,"c":1,"h":0.013250883392226132,"y":0.77031802127780657,"x":0.1460905474336632},{"y":0.78621908106096983,"x":0.14609053645274458,"h":0.013250883392226132,"c":1,"t":"reintroduce these changes from scratch while maintaining or even enhancing the","w":0.71193415323893228},{"w":0.26597137451171876,"c":1,"y":0.80053102366194329,"x":0.14383276004962775,"t":"desirable traits of wild strains.","h":0.017901072372957794},{"y":0.8459089558302203,"w":0.57209854125976567,"h":0.011516043098009354,"t":"* mutations: changes in an organism's genetic structure that can be passed down to later generations","c":1,"x":0.10077863920450085},{"t":"41","y":0.86773255796252025,"w":0.022633744875590001,"h":0.013081395583944722,"x":0.85802469124533254,"c":1},{"c":1,"h":0.03375352650564889,"y":0.95314993796778535,"t":"IELTSXpress.com","x":0.66991655033568553,"w":0.30612678527832038}]}